From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:24:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8010: Keep the GPIO domain powered for
 s2idle wake

The Power and Home buttons wake the system through the AP GPIO
controller. If PMGR powers its domain down during suspend-to-idle, the
wake interrupt never arrives and the system cannot be woken.

Keep the domain on and under manual control. The GPIO block is part of
the SoC, so this holds for every T8010 board. Verified on the iPad 6
(J71b): Power wakes it from s2idle on the installed system.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi
index 3db5b8e9b856..4680e312ed75 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -91,6 +91,8 @@ ps_gpio: power-controller@80118 {
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		label = "gpio";
+		apple,always-on; /* Power/Home wake IRQs over s2idle */
+		apple,manual-pm;
 	};
 
 	ps_pms: power-controller@80120 {
